{
 "id": "32562a96-9b99-4056-86be-ffa9f8bb82de",
 "type": "manga",
 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "100 Horror Stories about Marriage"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "結婚百怪談"
   },
   {
    "ja-ro": "Kekkon Hyaku Kaidan"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "In the past, it was said that if you married a sickly woman, you would have a lifetime of poor harvests. However, in modern times, it is okay for a woman to be thin, young-looking, timid, and ready to collapse at any moment. Sakuramachi Tamaki (24 years old) is the perfect woman for a man who likes weak women. Tamaki's stomach ulcer has healed and she finally goes to work, but she suddenly becomes dizzy and loses her footing down the stairs. She then marries the man she helped and is supposed to live a happy married life, but... Every time she has sex with her husband, her body deteriorates. But her unstoppable lust finally leads to the wife...!? This book contains 10 stories of bizarre horror that depict the messy relationships between men and women, focusing on episodes about married life! At the end of the book, there is a manga about the life of a manga artist by Tanimachi Yumeji and a commentary by Koga Shinichi, making it a very worthwhile read!"
  },
